<h1>CI/CD Integration</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Treat findings and incomplete evidence as distinct failure states.</p>

<h2>Direct CLI</h2>
<div class="code-block"><span class="kw">name</span>: Dependency evidence
<span class="kw">on</span>: [push, pull_request]
<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  <span class="kw">scan</span>:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/checkout@v4
      - <span class="kw">uses</span>: actions/setup-node@v4
        <span class="kw">with</span>:
          <span class="kw">node-version</span>: <span class="str">'22.13'</span>
      - <span class="kw">run</span>: npx @penumbraforge/vexes monitor --ci --severity high --no-user-config --no-project-config</div>

<p>The two config opt-outs make pull-request enforcement independent of repository and runner-account policy. Omit them only when those sources are part of the policy you intentionally trust.</p>

<h2>Composite Action</h2>
<div class="code-block">- <span class="kw">uses</span>: penumbraforge/vexes@v0
  <span class="kw">with</span>:
    <span class="kw">command</span>: scan
    <span class="kw">severity</span>: high
    <span class="kw">sarif-file</span>: vexes.sarif</div>
<p>A moving major tag is convenient, not immutable. High-assurance workflows should review and pin a verified commit SHA. The current Action runs the checked-out action code and isolates project/user config internally.</p>

<h2>SARIF</h2>
<div class="code-block">- <span class="kw">name</span>: Run vexes
  <span class="kw">run</span>: npx @penumbraforge/vexes monitor --ci --sarif --no-user-config --no-project-config &gt; results.sarif
  <span class="kw">continue-on-error</span>: true
- <span class="kw">name</span>: Upload SARIF
  <span class="kw">if</span>: always()
  <span class="kw">uses</span>: github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3
  <span class="kw">with</span>:
    <span class="kw">sarif_file</span>: results.sarif</div>
<p>Only upload a report that passed your validation and completeness policy. SARIF transports findings; it does not strengthen the underlying evidence.</p>

<h2>Deep evidence artifacts</h2>
<p><code>analyze --deep --json</code> deliberately returns incomplete/exit 2 when bounded sampling occurs. Use <code>continue-on-error</code> only to preserve the JSON artifact, then add an explicit policy step that distinguishes expected bounded coverage from execution or integrity failures.</p>

<h2>Exit codes</h2>
<table class="cmd-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Code</th><th>CI meaning</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>0</code></td><td>Requested supported checks complete with no finding at threshold; not a safety verdict</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>1</code></td><td>Finding met policy</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>2</code></td><td>Error or incomplete requested evidence; normally fail closed</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="info-box"><strong>Why exit 2 matters:</strong> network failure, unsupported input shape, unresolved source identity, or a requested bounded stage must not be flattened into “no findings.”</div>
